## Tone in visuals

Visual tone follows [VOICE.md](VOICE.md): the same restraint applies to
slides and charts as to prose — no decorative icons standing in for a
point that isn't made, no gradient-and-glow treatment to make a plain
fact look like an insight. Project-specific visual tells to avoid go
here: <e.g., "never use the corporate stock-photo handshake image">.

